13.9.1 Cleaning the names before matching
The names on the portal and in the payment register are written differently. One has “SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED”, the other “Shivam Constructions Pvt. Ltd.”. An exact join would find no match at all. So we first bring both to a common form, as in Chapter 20. We change to capitals, remove “M/s” and “(P)”, write “&” as “AND”, drop punctuation, and drop words like “Private”, “Limited” and “Co” that say nothing about who the firm is.

clean_firm &lt;- function(x) {
  x |&gt;
    str_to_upper() |&gt;
    str_remove("^M/S\\.?\\s*") |&gt;
    str_remove_all("\\(P\\)") |&gt;
    str_replace_all("&", " AND ") |&gt;
    str_replace_all("[[:punct:]]", " ") |&gt;
    str_squish() |&gt;
    str_remove_all("\\b(PRIVATE|PVT|LIMITED|LTD|AND CO|CO)\\b") |&gt;
    str_squish()
}

tibble(original = c("SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED", "M/s Shivam Constructions Pvt Ltd",
                    "Shivam Constructions (P) Ltd", "R. K. ELECTRICALS & CO.")) |&gt;
  mutate(cleaned = clean_firm(original))

# A tibble: 4 × 2
  original                             cleaned             
  &lt;chr&gt;                                &lt;chr&gt;               
1 SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS
2 M/s Shivam Constructions Pvt Ltd     SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS
3 Shivam Constructions (P) Ltd         SHIVAM CONSTRUCTIONS
4 R. K. ELECTRICALS & CO.              R K ELECTRICALS     


Now we match the cleaned names, and then check the dates. A payment is a concern only if it falls within the period of debarment.

debarred &lt;- debarred |&gt; mutate(name_key = clean_firm(firm))
payments &lt;- payments |&gt; mutate(name_key = clean_firm(payee))

name_matches &lt;- payments |&gt;
  inner_join(debarred, by = "name_key") |&gt;
  mutate(in_period = payment_date &gt;= from & payment_date &lt;= to) |&gt;
  select(voucher_no, payment_date, payee, amount, firm, from, to, in_period)
name_matches

