After cleaning, 5 payments match firms on the debarred list. But 3 of them were made outside the period of debarment. The first payment to Shivam Constructions was made before its debarment began on 1 July 2024. The payment to R K Electricals came before its debarment from 1 December 2024. Maa Durga Suppliers was paid after its debarment had ended in January 2024. These are not findings. Only the 2 payments to Shivam Constructions in August and October 2024 fall inside the period.

13.9.2 Names that cleaning does not catch
Cleaning removes differences of case, punctuation and legal form. It does not catch a name spelt differently, like “Vinayak Buildcon” for “Vinayaka Build Con”. For these we compare the names that did not match with every debarred name, and look at the closest ones. The Jaro-Winkler distance from stringdist (Chapter 35) is 0 for identical strings and grows towards 1 as they differ. We remove the spaces first, so that “BUILD CON” and “BUILDCON” are compared fairly.

unmatched &lt;- payments |&gt;
  anti_join(debarred, by = "name_key") |&gt;
  distinct(payee, name_key)

near_matches &lt;- cross_join(unmatched, debarred |&gt; select(firm, name_key, from, to),
                           suffix = c("_paid", "_debarred")) |&gt;
  mutate(distance = stringdist::stringdist(str_remove_all(name_key_paid, " "),
                                           str_remove_all(name_key_debarred, " "),
                                           method = "jw", p = 0.1)) |&gt;
  filter(distance &lt; 0.1) |&gt;
  arrange(distance)
near_matches |&gt; select(payee, firm, distance)

# A tibble: 1 × 3
  payee            firm               distance
  &lt;chr&gt;            &lt;chr&gt;                 &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Vinayak Buildcon Vinayaka Build Con   0.0125


Only one pair is close. The cut-off of 0.1 is a judgement, and every pair it finds must be checked by a person, as Chapter 35 explains. For a large list, the steps of Chapter 36 make such matching more reliable. Let us take the payments of this firm and check the period.

fuzzy_hits &lt;- payments |&gt;
  inner_join(near_matches |&gt; select(payee, firm, from, to), by = "payee") |&gt;
  filter(payment_date &gt;= from, payment_date &lt;= to) |&gt;
  select(voucher_no, payment_date, payee, amount, firm, from, to)
fuzzy_hits

# A tibble: 1 × 7
